# Optional overrides — checkpoint-mcp has no required env vars.
# Authentication is per-request via three request headers, matching MSPbots'
# own stored credential fields for this integration:
#   X-CheckPoint-Client-Id — Infinity Portal API Key Client ID
#   X-CheckPoint-Access-Key — Infinity Portal API Key Secret Key
#   X-CheckPoint-Region — the tenant's data-residency gateway base URL,
#     e.g. https://cloudinfra-gw-us.portal.checkpoint.com (US),
#     https://cloudinfra-gw.portal.checkpoint.com (EU), or
#     https://cloudinfra-gw.ap.portal.checkpoint.com (AP)
#
# This server performs a fresh 2-step login on every single tool call:
#   1. POST {region}/auth/external {clientId, accessKey} -> portal token
#      (valid 30 min)
#   2. POST {region}/app/endpoint-web-mgmt/harmony/endpoint/api/v1/session/login/cloud
#      with "Authorization: Bearer <portal token>" -> apiToken (valid ~6 min)
# Every real API call then needs BOTH "Authorization: Bearer <portal token>"
# AND "x-mgmt-api-token: <apiToken>" headers together. Nothing is cached or
# persisted across MCP calls.

MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
